{"study_accession":"PRJNA474387","secondary_study_accession":"SRP149638","title":"Comprehensive RNA-Seq profiling in PBMCs of ALS patients and healthy controls","description":"Coding and long non-coding RNA metabolism is now revealing its crucial role in Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS) pathogenesis. In this work, we performed Illumina RNA-seq analysis on Peripheral Blood Mononuclear Cells (PBMCs) from Sporadic and mutated ALS patients (mutations in FUS, TARDBP, SOD1, C9Orf72 and VCP genes) and healthy controls. Our aim is the whole-transcriptome characterization of PBMCs content, both in terms of coding and non coding RNAs, in order to compare the disease state to the healthy controls, both for sporadic patients and for mutated patients. Out dataset is a starting point for the omni-comprehensive analysis of coding and long non coding RNAs, from an easy to withdraw, manage and store tissue that shows to be a suitable model for RNA profiling in ALS. Overall design: whole transcriptome RNA-Seq profiling in PBMCs of ALS and healthy donors","pubmed":"30720798","geo_series":"","n_samples":11,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN09302595","study_accession":"PRJNA474387","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"healthy donor CTRL7","description":"healthy donor CTRL7","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3172787","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2018-07-05","attributes":[["source_name","healthy donor_blood"],["subject status","healthy donor"],["tissue","blood"],["cell_type","PBMC"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR7251670","experiment_accession":"SRX4156396","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":55298015,"base_count":16368212440,"first_public":"2018-07-05","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM3172787: healthy donor CTRL7 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN09302596","study_accession":"PRJNA474387","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"healthy do